WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.955 --> 00:00:03.462
(audience cheering)
- Thank you!

00:00:03.462 --> 00:00:04.396
(audience cheering)

00:00:04.396 --> 00:00:07.255
(audience cheering)
Oh my goodness.

00:00:07.255 --> 00:00:08.563
- I know!

00:00:08.563 --> 00:00:11.563
(audience cheering)

00:00:15.152 --> 00:00:16.471
- You guys.

00:00:16.471 --> 00:00:19.471
(audience cheering)

00:00:30.036 --> 00:00:32.889
- You guys know how to
make a lady feel welcome.

00:00:33.786 --> 00:00:35.469
- Okay.
- Where do we begin?

00:00:36.546 --> 00:00:38.316
Oh, which is like the book.

00:00:38.316 --> 00:00:41.736
- So this is my copy.
- Uh-huh.

00:00:41.736 --> 00:00:44.316
- And, as you know, on this show,

00:00:44.316 --> 00:00:49.316
we've tried to build something
that is whiplash comedy

00:00:50.826 --> 00:00:53.346
at one moment, because
we all need to laugh,

00:00:53.346 --> 00:00:54.696
and it's my survival

00:00:54.696 --> 00:00:56.436
and coping mechanism.
- Me too.

00:00:56.436 --> 00:00:59.304
- But we also wanna figure
out how to live a life here.

00:00:59.304 --> 00:01:01.266
- Mhmm, yeah.

00:01:01.266 --> 00:01:03.246
- And I can't think of anyone

00:01:03.246 --> 00:01:04.866
who I'd wanna hold a conversation

00:01:04.866 --> 00:01:08.144
about how to do such
a thing than with you.

00:01:08.144 --> 00:01:11.144
(audience cheering)

00:01:12.726 --> 00:01:16.386
Lately, I've been working
out a lot of stuff

00:01:16.386 --> 00:01:18.456
with my own life,

00:01:18.456 --> 00:01:23.226
and I appreciate my own
family and my mom so much.

00:01:23.226 --> 00:01:25.446
But when I was reading this book at night

00:01:25.446 --> 00:01:26.736
and coming home from work,

00:01:26.736 --> 00:01:27.846
which we take with us,

00:01:27.846 --> 00:01:30.036
so anyone who compartmentalizes,

00:01:30.036 --> 00:01:32.526
you know, personal and
professional, my hat's off to you,

00:01:32.526 --> 00:01:35.376
because usually it bleeds
all together for me.

00:01:35.376 --> 00:01:39.996
And I would hold your
book to my chest at night

00:01:39.996 --> 00:01:44.346
and I would wish that
I was in your family,

00:01:44.346 --> 00:01:46.926
that you were my mom or my sister,

00:01:46.926 --> 00:01:49.686
and I feel like everybody feels like that.

00:01:49.686 --> 00:01:53.166
My friend, who do you see
yourself as to everybody?

00:01:53.166 --> 00:01:56.586
- You know, I have never
thought about that in that way.

00:01:56.586 --> 00:02:00.006
I mean, I wanna be a support to people

00:02:00.006 --> 00:02:01.386
to the extent that I can.

00:02:01.386 --> 00:02:05.556
That's one of the reasons why
I wrote "The Light We Carry."

00:02:05.556 --> 00:02:08.166
Because I was, you know,

00:02:08.166 --> 00:02:11.316
in a time of uncertainty
when I wrote this book,

00:02:11.316 --> 00:02:13.479
in the middle of the quarantine,

00:02:14.736 --> 00:02:16.296
tucked away with my family.

00:02:16.296 --> 00:02:18.486
My girls had come home from college.

00:02:18.486 --> 00:02:20.946
They were afraid, like everybody else.

00:02:20.946 --> 00:02:23.766
And I had to think about what tools

00:02:23.766 --> 00:02:26.346
I had to lean on to get through.

00:02:26.346 --> 00:02:28.686
Because one of the
reasons why I'm so candid

00:02:28.686 --> 00:02:31.836
is that people think
that folks in high places

00:02:31.836 --> 00:02:33.726
have all the answers.

00:02:33.726 --> 00:02:36.636
We do not, we have a
lot of the same fears.

00:02:36.636 --> 00:02:39.066
All we have are the tools that we develop

00:02:39.066 --> 00:02:40.446
over the course of a lifetime.

00:02:40.446 --> 00:02:42.726
So I thought, "Well, let
me put this in a book."

00:02:42.726 --> 00:02:46.146
So I did my best to put
as much of the wisdom

00:02:46.146 --> 00:02:49.296
that I've accumulated
over this almost 60 years.

00:02:49.296 --> 00:02:51.069
Yes, January, 60.

00:02:51.905 --> 00:02:54.905
(audience clapping)

00:02:55.776 --> 00:03:00.776
And to share some of those
insights with my friends,

00:03:00.876 --> 00:03:04.206
my sisters, the people who look up to me,

00:03:04.206 --> 00:03:07.416
the people who are asking those questions.

00:03:07.416 --> 00:03:09.786
So I don't think it's one thing,

00:03:09.786 --> 00:03:12.216
it's kinda like whatever somebody needs

00:03:12.216 --> 00:03:14.676
to be able to hear something
that can help them.

00:03:14.676 --> 00:03:16.176
- Well, speaking of tools,

00:03:16.176 --> 00:03:18.846
I would like to ask you one for myself.

00:03:18.846 --> 00:03:21.956
- Yes.
- Funny story, I was with...

00:03:23.436 --> 00:03:25.479
- Michelle.
- Okay, thank you.

00:03:26.616 --> 00:03:30.006
I was with Michelle one morning.

00:03:30.006 --> 00:03:34.056
I was lucky enough to moderate
a beautiful discussion

00:03:34.056 --> 00:03:38.323
with children about something
me and my family love,

00:03:38.323 --> 00:03:39.993
"Waffle + Mochi."

00:03:41.016 --> 00:03:43.746
- [Michelle] The Netflix
special about food.

00:03:43.746 --> 00:03:44.916
It's a food adventure.

00:03:44.916 --> 00:03:46.956
- We connected, it was everything.

00:03:46.956 --> 00:03:49.626
I leave, I go about my day.

00:03:49.626 --> 00:03:52.866
And that evening I'm
at the George Clooney,

00:03:52.866 --> 00:03:56.586
George and Amal Clooney
Foundation Gala Awards.

00:03:56.586 --> 00:03:57.419
- Yeah.

00:03:57.419 --> 00:03:59.826
- And I see you across the room.

00:03:59.826 --> 00:04:04.826
You are with Meryl Streep,
John Oliver, George Clooney,

00:04:05.586 --> 00:04:07.266
and I think like a few other

00:04:07.266 --> 00:04:09.612
of the top functioning
people in the planet.

00:04:09.612 --> 00:04:12.996
(Michelle and Audience laughing)

00:04:12.996 --> 00:04:17.886
And I sat there and I didn't
know how to walk up to you.

00:04:17.886 --> 00:04:19.963
- Aw.
- I was like,

00:04:19.963 --> 00:04:22.776
"I think that's just too intimidating

00:04:22.776 --> 00:04:23.766
of a circle."

00:04:23.766 --> 00:04:25.566
- Well, you probably would've been blocked

00:04:25.566 --> 00:04:27.576
by an agent or something too.

00:04:27.576 --> 00:04:29.916
So I'm glad you didn't try

00:04:29.916 --> 00:04:32.136
and feel the hand of an agent.

00:04:32.136 --> 00:04:33.546
But you could've, you
know, and you should've.

00:04:33.546 --> 00:04:35.166
- Well, I'm single for seven years,

00:04:35.166 --> 00:04:37.204
so maybe it wouldn't have
been a bad thing, but.

00:04:37.204 --> 00:04:38.952
(Audience and Michelle laughing)

00:04:38.952 --> 00:04:41.304
(audience clapping)

00:04:41.304 --> 00:04:43.406
- [Michelle] And a lot of 'em are cute.

00:04:44.471 --> 00:04:47.054
(upbeat music)

